clipboard persistence are specced.\n4. **P4 — Mixed-DPI vertical-stacking bug** in `WaylandMonitorLayoutNormalizer.cs:69` — cumulative-physical-layout fix sketch with unit-test plan and an env-var escape hatch.\n5. **P5 — Ubuntu/Fedora docs parity**: INSTALL.md is Arch-only despite `package-linux.sh` already producing `.deb`/`.rpm`; plan includes copy-paste install/run commands and the critical XIP0044 dev caveat (portal hotkeys reject `dotnet run` binaries without a matching `.desktop` file).\n\nDeferred with rationale: `zxdg_exporter_v2` (Avalonia has no Wayland backend — app runs under XWayland, so the XID path suffices), AppImage (Flatpak is the universal answer), Flathub submission (human-led per XIP0075's provenance rules). KNOWN_ISSUES.md now points to the plan.\n\n### Rubric self-score (translation-layer RUBRIC.md)\n\n| Criterion | Score | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Outcome over activity | 2 | Named artifact at explicit path: \"Output primary artifact: …/docs/LINUX-IMPROVEMENT-PLAN.md\" — delivered there |\n| 2. Grounded references | 2 | All prompt paths verified 2026-06-12 (`flatpak/`, `native/`, `PORTING_GUIDE.md`, `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` all exist); plan cites file:line throughout |\n| 3. Testable done | 2 | All 5 done items binary-checked: plan exists ✓; ≥3-5 concrete patches (4 sketches + 1 applied) ✓; build/run instructions grounded in `package-linux.sh`/`XerahS.App` ✓; pushed via git-aoife ✓; this self-score ✓ |\n| 4. Executable verification | 2 | Prompt demanded repo-backed claims + explicit X/10; plan §6 gives concrete `busctl`/`gdbus`/log-grep commands per item |\n| 5. Scope boundaries | 2 | \"do NOT perform full builds / touch release pipelines\" honored — only the standalone 4.6s packaging-tool build; Windows behavior untouched |\n| 6. Workflow contract | 2 | git-aoife only, progressive commits (2), repo commit convention `[v0.23.105]` followed (props 0.23.105 > tag v0.23.99) |\n| 7. Failure handling | 2 | Wayland/X11 ambiguity handled via separat